    "user_request_original": "Design a 29-layer planar multilayer thin-film filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Stack sequence: alternating HfO2 and MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) layers starting with HfO2 adjacent to air, ending with HfO2 adjacent to substrate (15 HfO2 layers, 14 MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) layers). Initialize all layer thicknesses using quarter-wave optical thickness at 267.5 nm center wavelength (thickness_i = 267.5 nm / (4 * n_i) where n_i is the refractive index of layer material i), then apply ±15% multiplicative noise to create initial population diversity. Optimize all 29 individual layer thicknesses using gradient-based methods to maximize transmission in 255-280 nm band while minimizing transmission in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm bands. Total film layers must equal exactly 29. No metal layers allowed. Materials must be hfo2 and MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) only for film layers, SiO2 (Gao) for substrate. Evaluate at normal incidence unless otherwise specified in solver defaults.",
